docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:9:Phase 1 through Phase 7 will land as modules inside `lattice-core`, not as immediate sibling crates. The reserved crate names are still part of the contract: `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, and `lattice-verification`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:13:- `lattice-core` already owns the graph, storage, query, memory, indexing, and workflow types that these substrates must share.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:14:- The downstream Phase 1 and Phase 2 task files already target `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:18:## `lattice-core::identity`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:20:Reserved crate name: `lattice-identity`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:26:- identity value types and typed id encodings
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:27:- identity parser and serializer for MCP payloads
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:34:- `lattice-core::symbols`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:35:- `lattice-core::graph`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:36:- `lattice-core::storage`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:37:- `lattice-core::workspace`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:38:- `lattice-core::parser` for doc section and test identity extraction
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:40:Spec sections implemented: [### Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model), [## Storage Design](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design), and [## Fork Strategy](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#fork-strategy).
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:44:## `lattice-core::events`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:48:Purpose: Own the append-only event log, event payload hashing, replay readers, event compaction metadata, and workflow/session correlation. It records assistant and workflow activity through stable identities from `identity`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:53:- event envelope and referenced-identity fields
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:61:- `lattice-core::identity`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:62:- `lattice-core::storage`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:63:- `lattice-core::workspace`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:64:- `lattice-core::memory` only through narrow memory-id references, not memory retrieval
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:68:Boundary rationale: Events depend on identity and storage but remain below memory consolidation and retrieval. Replay readers may produce graph or memory rebuild inputs; they do not call high-level workflow code.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:70:## `lattice-core::memory_graph`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:74:Purpose: Own normalized memory classes, links, evidence, accesses, scores, contradiction/supersession semantics, and migration adapters from the existing `lattice-core::memory` row model.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:87:- `lattice-core::identity`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:88:- `lattice-core::events`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:89:- `lattice-core::memory`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:90:- `lattice-core::storage`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:91:- `lattice-core::workspace`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:97:## `lattice-core::retrieval`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:114:- `lattice-core::identity`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:115:- `lattice-core::events`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:116:- `lattice-core::memory_graph`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:117:- `lattice-core::graph`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:118:- `lattice-core::query`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:119:- `lattice-core::storage`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:120:- `lattice-core::intelligence` only through adapter traits during migration
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:124:Boundary rationale: Retrieval is above graph, event, memory, and identity storage. It must not be called by those lower modules, or the shared substrates would become cyclic and hard to test.
